[0.000000, "o", "Welcome to the Sonnet Checker!\r\n\r\nPlease choose a sonnet type:\r\n1. Shakespearean\r\n2. Petrarchan\r\n3. Spenserian\r\n"]
[1.000000, "o", "Enter your choice (1, 2, or 3): "]
[1.500000, "i", "1\n"]
[1.600000, "o", "Paste your sonnet, then press Enter twice to finish:\r\n"]
[2.200000, "i", "Shall I compare thee to a summer's day?\n"]
[2.800000, "i", "Thou art more lovely and more temperate:\n"]
[3.400000, "i", "Rough winds do shake the darling buds of May,\n"]
[4.000000, "i", "And summer's lease hath all too short a date;\n"]
[4.600000, "i", "Sometime too hot the eye of heaven shines,\n"]
[5.200000, "i", "And often is his gold complexion dimm'd;\n"]
[5.800000, "i", "And every fair from fair sometime declines,\n"]
[6.400000, "i", "By chance, or nature's changing course, untrimm'd;\n"]
[7.000000, "i", "But thy eternal summer shall not fade,\n"]
[7.600000, "i", "Nor lose possession of that fair thou ow'st,\n"]
[8.200000, "i", "Nor shall death brag thou wander'st in his shade,\n"]
[8.800000, "i", "When in eternal lines to time thou grow'st:\n"]
[9.400000, "i", "So long as men can breathe, or eyes can see,\n"]
[10.000000, "i", "So long lives this, and this gives life to thee.\n"]
[10.600000, "i", "\n"]
[11.200000, "o", "\r\nSonnet type: Shakespearean\r\n\r\nLine count [PASS]\r\n  14 / 14 lines\r\n\r\nRhyme scheme [FAIL]\r\n  expected: A B A B C D C D E F E F G G\r\n  detected: A B A C D ? D ? E ? E ? F F\r\n  end words: day, temperate, May, date, shines, dimm'd, declines, untrimm'd, fade, ow'st, shade, grow'st, see, thee\r\n\r\nMeter [PASS] (10 syllables/line, iambic pentameter)\r\n  line  1: 10 syllables\r\n  line  2: 9 syllables\r\n  line  3: 10 syllables\r\n  line  4: 10 syllables\r\n  line  5: 10 syllables\r\n  line  6: 10 syllables\r\n  line  7: 10 syllables\r\n  line  8: 10 syllables\r\n  line  9: 10 syllables\r\n  line 10: 10 syllables\r\n  line 11: 10 syllables\r\n  line 12: 10 syllables\r\n  line 13: 10 syllables\r\n  line 14: 10 syllables\r\n\r\nOverall: FAIL\r\n"]